      "pText": "Paheli is a puzzle-themed play structure where jigsaw pieces become the climbing route. A purple puzzle tower stands at the centre, puzzle-shaped climbers lead up its sides, and a huge puzzle piece at the back gives another way to the top. Two slides, one yellow and one orange, bring children down. Working out which piece to climb next builds problem solving and concentration. It is meant for ages 5 to 12 and takes up to 15 children. The product area is 21'7\" x 12'10\" and the safe play area is 27'7\" x 17'10\". Climbing, hanging and sliding also build upper body strength. It comes in a multi-colour finish. The structure has a 3-year warranty on its main materials. Send us your site photos."
